/-!
# Local cohomology along a locally Koszul-regular closed subset vanishes off its codimension

Let `X` be a scheme and let `Z ⊆ X` be a closed subset which can locally be cut out by a
Koszul-regular sequence of `c` elements of the structure sheaf.  Then the local cohomology
sheaves of a flat quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` vanish outside degree `c`:

`ℋ ^i_Z(ℱ) = 0` for `i ≠ c`.

This is **Stacks 0G7P** in full.  The two halves are proved separately and then joined:

* above degree `c` the hypotheses play no role and the statement is Stacks 0G7N, already
  available as `isZero_homology_derivedSupportedSections_of_locallyKoszulRegular` in the
  namespace `Stacks.Perfect.LocalCohomologyDegrees`;
* below degree `c` both hypotheses are needed.  For `c` *global* equations whose restrictions to
  the affine opens are Koszul-regular this is
  `Stacks.Perfect.KoszulFlatVanishing.isZero_homology_derivedSupportedSections_of_lt`, and what is
  added here is the passage from global to local equations.

That passage is the argument of Stacks 0G7N: a sheaf vanishes as soon as it vanishes on an open
cover, local cohomology is computed on a resolution by injectives, and restriction to an open
subscheme is exact, preserves injectives and takes the subsheaf of sections supported on `Z` to
the subsheaf of sections supported on the preimage of `Z`.  Over one open of the cover the
equations are global and the global-equations statement applies.

## The reading of "locally"

The hypothesis below asks for an **affine** open neighbourhood carrying the Koszul-regular
sequence.  By **Stacks 063G** that is equivalent to the source's "locally": a sheaf of ideals is
Koszul-regular — generated on *some* open neighbourhood of each point by a Koszul-regular
sequence — exactly when each point of the support has an affine open neighbourhood on which it is
generated by a Koszul-regular sequence.  The affine form is the one the mathematics uses, here as
in the source, whose proof "boils down to" a statement about a ring `R`; and it is the form that
restricts, Koszul-regularity of a sequence in `Γ(U, 𝒪)` for a *non-affine* `U` saying nothing
about its restrictions, since `Γ(U, 𝒪) → Γ(V, 𝒪)` is then not flat.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlat_restrictFunctor`: restriction to an open subscheme preserves flatness
  of a quasi-coherent module.
* `Stacks.Perfect.LocalCohomologyDegrees.isKoszulRegular_restrictOpen_of_isAffine`: a
  Koszul-regular sequence of global functions on an affine scheme restricts to a Koszul-regular
  sequence on every affine open.
* `isZero_homology_derivedSupportedSections_of_locallyKoszulRegular_of_lt`, in the namespace
  `Stacks.Perfect.LocalCohomologyDegrees`: the vanishing below degree `c`.
* `isZero_homology_derivedSupportedSections_of_locallyKoszulRegular_of_ne`, in the namespace
  `Stacks.Perfect.LocalCohomologyDegrees`: **Stacks 0G7P**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G7P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G7P)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G7N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G7N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G7M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G7M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
-/

